# Rules of the talks
- The delegations speak in turn. Each delegation has at most {{ max_rounds }} messages. If there is no agreement after that, the talks end without a deal.
- In every message, state your current complete proposal on all six issues in plain words, and explain or argue for it.
- To accept, set "decision" to "accept", put the exact terms you accept in "accepted_terms" (normally the other delegation's latest proposal), and say clearly in your message that you accept and on which terms.
- A deal is concluded only when both delegations have accepted the same terms. If the other delegation has just accepted, you conclude the deal by accepting the same terms; if you want changes, make a new proposal instead.
- You may leave the talks by setting "decision" to "walk_away".
- Keep each message under 150 words. Write it as a diplomat speaking to the other delegation.

# Your reply
Reply with a single JSON object and nothing else:
- "message": your message to the other delegation, written in {{ dialog_language }}.
- "my_offer": your current complete proposal: the option number for each issue, under the issue's key.
- "their_offer_as_understood": the other delegation's latest proposal as you understood it, as option numbers (null for any issue they did not make clear, or for all issues before they have spoken).
- "decision": "continue", "accept" or "walk_away".
- "accepted_terms": the option numbers you accept if "decision" is "accept", otherwise null.
- "plan": a private note to yourself, at most 40 words, in English. The other delegation never sees it.
